    "lineage": "pyproject.toml description: 'Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve'. CLAUDE.md: 'open-source implementation of Google DeepMind's AlphaEvolve system'. The README at this pin does not mention AlphaEvolve, FunSearch or DeepMind by name; it cites an HF blog 'Towards Open Evolutionary Agents'. Evolution operators named in README: MAP-Elites, island model with ring-topology migration, double selection (performance vs inspiration), artifact side-channel; OptiLLM (same author) as optional proxy. || main loop (reader, from the code): ProcessParallelController.run_evolution samples a parent and inspirations from an island (exploration from island / exploitation from archive / random, by exploration_ratio+exploitation_ratio), ships a DB snapshot to a worker that builds a prompt, calls the LLM ensemble, applies SEARCH/REPLACE diffs (or full rewrite) to the parent, evaluates the child, and returns it; the parent process adds the child to the MAP-Elites island database, migrates between islands when due, checkpoints, and repeats until max_iterations, target_score or early stopping."
   },
   "basis": "TECHNE_RECORD"
  },
